WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.602 --> 00:00:02.489
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update!

00:00:02.489 --> 00:00:05.271
And, in&nbsp;this video, I'm going to show you our biggest problems.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:06.427
Or, challenges...

00:00:06.427 --> 00:00:07.436
And, we're going to do&nbsp;a Q&amp;A.

00:00:07.436 --> 00:00:10.464
So, we're going to answer some questions 
from you guys, at the end of this video.

00:00:10.464 --> 00:00:13.703
And every eighth video, and I actually do this wrong all the time...

00:00:13.703 --> 00:00:17.691
It's not every eighth video,
but every tenth video, but then the eighth of it...

00:00:17.691 --> 00:00:22.847
So, number 8, 18, 28, 38, and now we're in number 48.

00:00:22.847 --> 00:00:23.960
This is number 58...

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.197
Number 68...

00:00:25.197 --> 00:00:27.259
So, here we are: update number 78!

00:00:27.259 --> 00:00:31.620
The first eighth-problem-video,
of Project Kamp season 3!

00:00:35.826 --> 00:00:39.224
So, Season 3 already started 
and we have a&nbsp;few challenges popping up...

00:00:39.446 --> 00:00:43.476
But, before we go into the new ones,
let me put a bit of context with the&nbsp;old ones.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:44.794
And, how they relate to each other...

00:00:44.794 --> 00:00:49.702
In Season 1, we had a lot of practical challenges, 
and some&nbsp;were pretty easy to solve.

00:00:49.702 --> 00:00:51.099
Cleaning the road, an address...

00:00:51.099 --> 00:00:52.831
We don't really have a place to sit...

00:00:52.831 --> 00:00:54.570
Some were&nbsp;a bit more complex...

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.956
So, we need to get water to hook up these containers...

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.376
"Do you have electricity?", and&nbsp;they said: "Yeah, it's easy!"

00:00:59.376 --> 00:01:02.244
So, I would say the video making is kind of a challenge actually...

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.160
And, some, we still don't really have a solution for...

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.022
Quite a thing having all these flies...

00:01:07.022 --> 00:01:08.178
Highway sounds.

00:01:08.178 --> 00:01:09.967
And, in&nbsp;Season 2, we had people come in.

00:01:09.967 --> 00:01:12.044
Which, also, brought some new practical challenges.

00:01:12.392 --> 00:01:13.657
Somewhat easy&nbsp;to fix.

00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:15.086
Doing a lot of paperwork...

00:01:15.086 --> 00:01:17.480
This beautiful purple Caddy.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:19.380
Our chairs keep breaking...

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.991
But, we also&nbsp;got a few bigger challenges coming up, like fire risk.

00:01:22.991 --> 00:01:25.260
Which is now part of our long-term planning.

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:28.648
And now, Season 3: more people coming...

00:01:28.648 --> 00:01:31.197
So, the challenges are more about scaling up.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:33.814
So, on the one&nbsp;hand, we have all the practical challenges.

00:01:33.814 --> 00:01:36.638
Which, by now, we're not too scared of those anymore.

00:01:37.081 --> 00:01:40.222
But, we&nbsp;also have some more human challenges popping up...

00:01:40.222 --> 00:01:42.320
And, let's start off with practical ones!

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.559
So, this&nbsp;year we are scaling up.

00:01:46.559 --> 00:01:52.689
At our peak moment, we will be with 25 people,
 which means that it's 10 more&nbsp;people, than last year...

00:01:52.689 --> 00:01:56.648
More people, more food, more projects, more tools...

00:01:57.028 --> 00:01:59.336
That means: also more need&nbsp;for storage...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.473
We have this container here, that we built for storage.

00:02:03.473 --> 00:02:05.816
Which, at the moment, it's just a&nbsp;dump place...

00:02:05.816 --> 00:02:10.545
We still need to think of a very smart way,
 of dividing the container in three places.

00:02:10.545 --> 00:02:15.468
How to store materials, how to store tools,
 and how to store food.

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.485
And, we don't know how to do&nbsp;that for now...

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:24.600
This brings us to our next challenge,
 which is our old storage place: this white tent.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.040
As&nbsp;you can see, this is kind of a mess...

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.431
We have boxes of veggies, that we get weekly.

00:02:32.431 --> 00:02:34.596
A funky trash&nbsp;system...

00:02:35.198 --> 00:02:36.227
Oranges...

00:02:36.544 --> 00:02:38.606
We have all of these windows!

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.360
Concrete!

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.751
We don't really know how to continue&nbsp;with this...

00:02:44.751 --> 00:02:46.138
We already repaired the windows.

00:02:46.138 --> 00:02:48.168
The frame is kind of okay...

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.959
Not super stable.

00:02:49.959 --> 00:02:56.804
But,&nbsp;we are questioning if we keep the frame,
 and put another fabric on top.

00:02:56.804 --> 00:02:58.651
Do we use this&nbsp;for storage?

00:02:58.651 --> 00:03:01.044
Do we use this for shade for the people?

00:03:01.044 --> 00:03:02.798
Do we not use this at all?

00:03:02.798 --> 00:03:06.654
We don't know,&nbsp;and it's an ongoing challenge,
 that we need to figure out...

00:03:07.034 --> 00:03:11.173
One of the places, that we are still&nbsp;
within the black hole, is in the waste system...

00:03:11.173 --> 00:03:15.681
We have so many cultures, 
and in each country we&nbsp;recycle differently.

00:03:15.681 --> 00:03:19.908
So, for example, for many people: this is not recyclable.

00:03:19.908 --> 00:03:24.020
In some places in&nbsp;Portugal, this is recyclable, 
and in some others it's not.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:28.617
For some people, like, this is clearly plastic, but it's dirty...

00:03:28.617 --> 00:03:30.003
So, where do you put it?

00:03:30.003 --> 00:03:35.118
So, we are trying to figure out like a simple system,
that people can easily follow.

00:03:35.118 --> 00:03:40.759
And, that we can have a clear, 
and clean system for the waste.

00:03:40.759 --> 00:03:43.500
We are with more people, and we create more waste!

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:55.994
One of the challenges, of 20 people living off-grid,
 in this setting, is the electricity.

00:03:55.994 --> 00:04:01.407
Because, our electricity consumption scales up,
 with the&nbsp;amount of people we are here.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:08.689
If we don't have sun, for more than three or four days,
 our electricity&nbsp;starts to be tight...

00:04:08.689 --> 00:04:14.628
We could scale up our solar energy,
 but this comes with some challenges...

00:04:14.628 --> 00:04:20.002
As&nbsp;like, balancing out our capacity for storage,
 and our capacity of production...

00:04:20.002 --> 00:04:25.195
So, depending on the&nbsp;time of the year,
 we would need more or less of that.

00:04:25.195 --> 00:04:29.334
The number of people&nbsp;is also not stable, 
that is in the camp during the year...

00:04:29.619 --> 00:04:36.581
So, we're in the process of trying to scale,
 but we need to find&nbsp;the right amount.

00:04:36.993 --> 00:04:40.698
We could introduce the wind power, here in the Kamp.

00:04:40.698 --> 00:04:50.083
We are actually working together with a company, 
that makes recycled plastic, open-source, wind turbines in Belgium.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:54.427
Trying to figure it out&nbsp;if that would be convenient,
 for us to install in the Kamp.

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:56.687
But, this comes with several challenges...

00:04:56.687 --> 00:05:01.645
We are surrounded by mimosas for example, 
that grow two to three meters a year...

00:05:01.645 --> 00:05:06.120
Which, also changes the wind speed that we have now, in Basekamp.

00:05:06.595 --> 00:05:11.102
It would come with a noisy, big wind turbine.

00:05:11.102 --> 00:05:13.705
If we would install it in another part of the Kamp...

00:05:13.705 --> 00:05:19.325
We would need to dig a cable of many meters depending...

00:05:20.149 --> 00:05:24.345
But, this would come also with a loss of energy on the way...

00:05:25.359 --> 00:05:31.254
Hydro-electric power is something that many people suggested us 
in the comments, after seeing the waterfall.

00:05:31.729 --> 00:05:35.988
But, what&nbsp;happens is that the waterfall is not in our land...

00:05:35.988 --> 00:05:39.536
So, that part of the of land doesn't&nbsp;belong to us...

00:05:39.536 --> 00:05:45.219
It wouldn't be convenient to install a new electric station there for us...

00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:51.370
It's also around half a kilometer away from our battery storage.

00:05:52.225 --> 00:05:56.996
Which, it would come with energy loss on the way...

00:05:56.996 --> 00:05:58.181
Where do we put a cable?

00:05:58.181 --> 00:05:59.475
Is it in the air?

00:05:59.475 --> 00:06:01.116
Do we need to dig it?

00:06:01.686 --> 00:06:07.745
A lot of challenges to come here with installations,
and we are still in a temporary setup...

00:06:07.745 --> 00:06:15.161
So, our capacity to install these kind of 
fixed&nbsp;electricity suppliers is quite low nowadays...

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:26.078
So, we're scaling up!

00:06:26.078 --> 00:06:28.032
Which, it means that systems are&nbsp;getting pushed...

00:06:28.444 --> 00:06:31.797
Which includes, not having enough dried towels...

00:06:31.797 --> 00:06:37.097
Maybe the week is overcrowded,
and there is not enough bread, because the bread gets eaten too fast...

00:06:37.921 --> 00:06:42.564
We also got some washing basins, 
but the&nbsp;water gets too dirty easily...

00:06:42.564 --> 00:06:44.442
Our compost bin -- too tiny.

00:06:44.949 --> 00:06:47.453
But, all of them are quite easy to solve!

00:06:47.928 --> 00:06:48.804
They're quite practical!

00:06:48.804 --> 00:06:52.499
We just take a bigger compost bin...

00:06:52.499 --> 00:06:54.240
Buy some new towels...

00:06:55.317 --> 00:06:58.452
Install a bread team that bakes more bread...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.313
And, maybe, some new dishwasher buckets.

00:07:02.883 --> 00:07:03.782
Easy to solve!

00:07:03.782 --> 00:07:06.734
But, there is one bigger&nbsp;problem, which is a bit shitty...

00:07:06.734 --> 00:07:08.143
Let me show you!

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.238
So, this brings us to the toilet...

00:07:12.238 --> 00:07:15.380
The toilet is&nbsp;getting quite crowded, 
especially during the rush hours...

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:18.091
This means that we would like a new toilet.

00:07:18.091 --> 00:07:20.580
But, finding the expert for it, it's quite a challenge...

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:22.509
It's not the biggest challenge...

00:07:22.509 --> 00:07:23.625
We have a&nbsp;bigger one!

00:07:23.625 --> 00:07:24.692
A shittier one even.

00:07:24.882 --> 00:07:25.810
Let me show you!

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:30.339
All right!

00:07:30.339 --> 00:07:31.970
This brings us to the core of the&nbsp;problem...

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:34.190
The poo area we are in now...

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:37.456
The poohole of Season 1 got filled up half...

00:07:37.456 --> 00:07:40.330
In Season 2, we&nbsp;filled up one-and-a-half poohole...

00:07:40.837 --> 00:07:45.344
And, in the third season, we already filled up the first one, 
and we&nbsp;just started!

00:07:45.882 --> 00:07:47.713
This shows how big the problem is!

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.880
Come, and let me show you,
what the&nbsp;system looks like at the moment...

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:59.226
Currently, we are dropping a bucket of&nbsp;poo,
 into this hole every time...

00:07:59.226 --> 00:08:03.214
Cover it a bit with soil, and some sawdust, to dry it out.

00:08:03.214 --> 00:08:05.253
But, the smell increases&nbsp;during summer...

00:08:05.253 --> 00:08:07.011
We don't really know what to do with it.

00:08:07.835 --> 00:08:13.152
The area is also covered by rocks,
which makes&nbsp;it hard for us to dig new holes...

00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:17.782
So, what we would like to ask you: 
"What to do with all this poo?"

00:08:18.321 --> 00:08:21.268
We're opening a research module on the website!

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:26.280
Let's see if we can find a solution!

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:34.808
Almost a thorn in my butt!

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:36.914
So, currently, we live&nbsp;in Basekamp.

00:08:36.914 --> 00:08:41.578
And, most of the problems you just saw, 
we hope to address them, when we build&nbsp;the Community Center.

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:45.506
Because, this building would hold many complex infrastructure.

00:08:45.506 --> 00:08:48.198
Energy&nbsp;systems, sewage, water, showers...

00:08:48.198 --> 00:08:49.378
It would all be in here!

00:08:49.378 --> 00:08:53.125
And, this project is currently in the process of legalization.

00:08:53.125 --> 00:08:55.629
We would also need to find funding for that soon-ish..

00:08:55.629 --> 00:08:58.461
Which, it's going to be a next big challenge we're going to have...

00:08:58.461 --> 00:09:01.689
But, what this building doesn't&nbsp;have is places to sleep...

00:09:01.689 --> 00:09:05.847
This would just be the shared facilities,
 for the people to be at during the day.

00:09:05.847 --> 00:09:07.997
But, at night, we need houses...

00:09:07.997 --> 00:09:12.357
And, this year, in Season 3, for the first time:
we're going to build our Level 2-house.

00:09:12.864 --> 00:09:17.130
And, for that, I actually have a special request for you guys,
 which should be kind of fun!

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:18.327
Let me show you!

00:09:21.201 --> 00:09:26.160
So, the goal is to make a house, 
that&nbsp;is more proper than a tent, but still movable.

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:29.380
So, you don't have all the complexity of the legal&nbsp;paperwork...

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:32.324
We figured: let's build it on top of a big trailer!

00:09:32.324 --> 00:09:34.665
So, me and Adrian went to visit the&nbsp;scrapyard.

00:09:34.665 --> 00:09:38.786
And, we started looking into different kinds of trailers,
 and boxes that are on top.

00:09:39.134 --> 00:09:41.816
And,&nbsp;we found five, different, cool options!

00:09:42.545 --> 00:09:43.916
Each has their pros and cons.

00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:46.811
Some are good for documentation, and others are more fun.

00:09:46.811 --> 00:09:52.136
And, we couldn't decide, so, we figured you guys can decide, 
what house we're going&nbsp;to build up!

00:09:52.136 --> 00:09:53.406
So, let me show you the options.

00:09:53.406 --> 00:09:54.754
This is the first option!

00:09:54.754 --> 00:09:56.353
It's an old pig trailer.

00:09:56.353 --> 00:09:57.581
This&nbsp;is Adrian here in front.

00:09:57.581 --> 00:10:00.031
This container is in very rough condition...

00:10:00.031 --> 00:10:02.707
It's been there for a long time...

00:10:02.707 --> 00:10:05.097
It requires lots of work, but it's quite unique!

00:10:05.097 --> 00:10:08.000
It's a good size, and it's an old trailer!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.948
Very specific, so&nbsp;it's hard to replicate...

00:10:11.138 --> 00:10:14.581
But, realistically, I don't think anyone else would ever buy that trailer...

00:10:14.581 --> 00:10:17.789
So,&nbsp;it would just rot away, so that would be good,
if we would use it!

00:10:18.296 --> 00:10:22.239
And, it's somewhat exciting to&nbsp;start this one,
 because it's bit of an unknown.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:25.404
Second option: a shipping container!

00:10:25.404 --> 00:10:26.805
You know these&nbsp;things...

00:10:26.805 --> 00:10:28.595
You can get one in a pretty good state!

00:10:28.595 --> 00:10:31.958
It's not too much work, because the outer walls&nbsp;are super good!

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:33.772
It's a good size!

00:10:33.772 --> 00:10:37.990
We already have a bunch of them in Basekamp 
which is also the downside a&nbsp;little bit...

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:40.400
Like, it's less fun here...

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:45.733
But, they're useful for documentation,&nbsp;
because everyone can find shipping containers&nbsp;around the world.

00:10:45.733 --> 00:10:49.620
So, having a blueprint of&nbsp;a house of a container is somewhat useful...

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:55.103
And, it's kind of easy to build, but&nbsp;also not very challenging...

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:57.843
So, option number three is this fridge box!

00:10:57.843 --> 00:11:02.507
Which you can sometimes see&nbsp;on the back of trailers, 
where they put in some ice creams, or when they're cooling things.

00:11:03.616 --> 00:11:07.229
You find&nbsp;these boxes in pretty good state, the one we saw.

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:14.382
It's kind of dirty work to work with this,
because it's all polyester, fiberglass, and&nbsp;polyurethane foam...

00:11:14.382 --> 00:11:22.093
So, with chemical stuff to work with, especially on the land,
 you could see it looking ugly on a piece of land.

00:11:23.043 --> 00:11:28.321
But, I would&nbsp;say it's very useful to document, 
because there are many of these boxes around the world.

00:11:28.321 --> 00:11:30.874
I don't think&nbsp;any of those get recycled...

00:11:30.874 --> 00:11:36.436
So, we could really use some good examples of what to do with that,
instead of that they get burned...

00:11:36.436 --> 00:11:39.643
And, I'm also not sure if it's nice to actually live in these things...

00:11:39.643 --> 00:11:42.060
With all the fiberglass, and polyurethane around...

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:46.150
So, it feels like it might need some research, 
but&nbsp;it's an option as well...

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:48.545
If you guys think that's what we should do.

00:11:49.527 --> 00:11:53.792
Option number four is a&nbsp;transport box,
 and this one is in pretty good state!

00:11:53.792 --> 00:11:59.461
It's quite some work, because currently it looks&nbsp;like it has walls,
 but this is just this canvas material...

00:11:59.778 --> 00:12:02.567
So, you need to build an inner, and an&nbsp;outer wall...

00:12:02.567 --> 00:12:05.085
But, it would be a very clean base!

00:12:05.085 --> 00:12:08.458
It's a good size, and also nice height inside!

00:12:08.458 --> 00:12:10.912
And, it seems&nbsp;somewhat useful as well to replicate!

00:12:10.912 --> 00:12:14.518
Because, this is a very common truck trailer around the world.

00:12:14.518 --> 00:12:16.551
So, you would easily find it, and it's pretty standardized.

00:12:17.248 --> 00:12:19.122
But, it does need a lot of new materials...

00:12:19.122 --> 00:12:22.597
Like, you don't have any walls that you can reuse...

00:12:24.072 --> 00:12:26.426
We could reuse the tarp, so that's cool!

00:12:27.725 --> 00:12:30.913
All&nbsp;right, option number five: this old blue metal box.

00:12:30.913 --> 00:12:33.064
It's in a pretty good state!

00:12:33.064 --> 00:12:36.432
It's from the Belgium&nbsp;taxes, I think, or the customs? 

00:12:37.794 --> 00:12:41.342
And, the size is pretty good inside, although it's a bit low

00:12:41.342 --> 00:12:45.242
So,&nbsp;it would be nice to extend the roof,
 but the roof will probably need to be replaced anyway...

00:12:46.003 --> 00:12:49.929
But, the&nbsp;whole outer walls we can use,
 so we only have to build the inner walls.

00:12:49.929 --> 00:12:52.403
Which saves a lot of time...

00:12:52.403 --> 00:12:55.351
And, it's a bit less specific in documentation.

00:12:55.351 --> 00:12:58.936
So, I don't think you necessarily found another box,&nbsp;
like this, around the world...

00:12:58.936 --> 00:13:02.069
But, the principle would be to build a house inside of a box.

00:13:02.512 --> 00:13:06.834
And, they actually&nbsp;had a similar box here 
as well, from the German circus -- a white one...

00:13:06.834 --> 00:13:10.586
So, that's also an option, but&nbsp;they're the same kind of build...

00:13:10.586 --> 00:13:12.321
You just have this metal outer wall.

00:13:13.176 --> 00:13:16.316
So, this one is pretty neutral, not wild, not boring...

00:13:16.316 --> 00:13:17.701
Yeah, it's an option...

00:13:18.366 --> 00:13:21.698
So, now on Patreon, you can vote which option we should go&nbsp;for.

00:13:21.698 --> 00:13:23.652
And, we'll pick whatever comes out of the votes.

00:13:24.032 --> 00:13:27.616
Kind of scary to do, but, yeah, 
I hope it's going&nbsp;to be okay.

00:13:27.616 --> 00:13:30.625
And, if you're not a Patreon you could become one, which is cool!

00:13:30.625 --> 00:13:32.273
Because, you would also support&nbsp;the project.

00:13:32.273 --> 00:13:34.175
Or, leave your comment below.

00:13:34.175 --> 00:13:35.319
So, then other Patreons can see it...

00:13:35.319 --> 00:13:39.631
And, they can vote to see what&nbsp;
the rest of the world kind of likes in there.

00:13:39.631 --> 00:13:43.950
And, the reasons for doing this, is to actually try&nbsp;out,
to have a bit more of a distributed decision making.

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:47.456
So, it's not just the people in the Kamp&nbsp;deciding, but a bigger audience.

00:13:47.456 --> 00:13:49.050
Which, in this case, it's Patreon.

00:13:49.367 --> 00:13:52.637
So, if you want to explore, if you can&nbsp;integrate this, 
and do this more in the future...

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:57.033
Anyways, these were all our practical challenges we currently have...

00:13:57.603 --> 00:14:00.814
So, now, let's go to a few more human challenges

00:14:00.814 --> 00:14:05.670
Which are going to be a little bit more&nbsp;
complex and difficult to explain, so bear with us...

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:12.051
So, about human challenges...

00:14:12.051 --> 00:14:17.340
It is about&nbsp;how to regulate different types of energy.

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:24.380
This means: for the people that are here short-term,
 they come with a boost of energy!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:28.782
And, they leave all the world and reality that they know&nbsp;behind.

00:14:28.782 --> 00:14:31.621
They just give everything to Project Kamp!

00:14:31.621 --> 00:14:35.298
And, this only happens, because of the people&nbsp;
that come from the outside.

00:14:35.298 --> 00:14:36.540
So, a massive thank you!

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:42.762
For us, that stay here for a longer term,
 we are&nbsp;just creating our lives here.

00:14:42.762 --> 00:14:45.636
So, we are also holding a big responsibility!

00:14:45.636 --> 00:14:51.390
And, we are asking questions on how to separate 
work for just a leisure moment.

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:57.464
At the moment, we can't really&nbsp;do that very easily,
because we all sleep in Basekamp.

00:14:57.464 --> 00:15:05.759
We all eat in Basekamp, we all work in&nbsp;Basekamp,
and we all just are living around in Basekamp.

00:15:05.759 --> 00:15:11.501
So, we are trying to figure out&nbsp;ways, 
that we can balance out this quest.

00:15:11.501 --> 00:15:18.870
And, think of strategies that we can integrate,
and stay here more energized longer terms.

00:15:21.553 --> 00:15:22.845
So, there is a big challenge...

00:15:22.845 --> 00:15:30.228
Which,&nbsp;is finding a balance in between finding a way,
to align everything towards the&nbsp;goal of the project...

00:15:30.228 --> 00:15:32.938
Having people come in that we all care about...

00:15:32.938 --> 00:15:36.202
But then, also, having our personal&nbsp;needs...

00:15:36.202 --> 00:15:38.520
And, to balance it out, is very difficult.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:44.300
This was already difficult within Season 2, 
but&nbsp;now in Season 3, it only becomes bigger...

00:15:44.648 --> 00:15:45.764
So, this is nothing new.

00:15:45.764 --> 00:15:47.964
We already talked about this during the winter.

00:15:47.964 --> 00:15:51.716
But, to bring this in practice, it's still a hard thing to do...

00:15:52.033 --> 00:15:56.610
At some point, you just get absorbed by the responsibilities
 and you forget about yourself...

00:15:56.610 --> 00:15:59.965
But, we found some techniques,
and some&nbsp;ways to at least improve it.

00:15:59.965 --> 00:16:04.161
Which is: leaving the land every now and then,
 or talking with each&nbsp;other...

00:16:04.161 --> 00:16:08.506
Maybe, taking your time for yourself,
 and finding out what is that what you need.

00:16:09.203 --> 00:16:14.626
Okay, but&nbsp;it's still hard to bring in practice, because we're all
 in a small space, and you get carried away by things...

00:16:14.626 --> 00:16:17.494
So, sometimes, we're just not able to solve something...

00:16:17.494 --> 00:16:20.044
Or, need to say no at a certain point...

00:16:20.804 --> 00:16:22.258
Which, is not really nice...

00:16:22.258 --> 00:16:26.483
You feel bad, it make you feel stressed,
 which comes on top of already&nbsp;not feeling good...

00:16:26.863 --> 00:16:28.086
It's not an easy challenge.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:33.609
We are working on it, but hopefully,
 in&nbsp;the future, this will clear up.

00:16:33.609 --> 00:16:34.720
That's it.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:42.158
So, finally, one last human challenge 
is all of&nbsp;you guys watching these videos!

00:16:43.711 --> 00:16:46.611
Because, we want to make good videos, but it's kind of&nbsp;hard...

00:16:46.611 --> 00:16:48.649
Because, the audience is very diverse!

00:16:48.649 --> 00:16:53.236
So, we have people subscribing since Season 1,
when I was just one guy chopping some bushes here... 

00:16:53.806 --> 00:16:58.602
Or, people subscribing now in Season 3,
where it's way more people, and bigger projects going on!

00:16:59.014 --> 00:17:03.282
So, the audience is quite diverse,
and then people also just have different preferences.

00:17:03.282 --> 00:17:04.867
Some like fast videos...

00:17:04.867 --> 00:17:06.224
Some like&nbsp;a lot of timelapses...

00:17:06.224 --> 00:17:11.037
Some like loud music, some soft, 
which is a recurring topic in the&nbsp;comments.

00:17:11.385 --> 00:17:14.605
Which makes it kind of hard for us to know what it is...

00:17:14.605 --> 00:17:19.308
What does a good video look&nbsp;like, 
and how can we consistently deliver that?

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:21.298
Now, we do have a cool video team here!

00:17:21.298 --> 00:17:23.100
These two guys are editing the videos!

00:17:25.355 --> 00:17:28.429
But, even that is not super consistent...

00:17:28.429 --> 00:17:30.300
Because, they don't know what they're doing next year.

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:35.196
Javier might start a tomato farm, 
and Guilherme might start a repair drone shop...

00:17:35.196 --> 00:17:36.515
It could easily be the case!

00:17:36.515 --> 00:17:42.145
So, it's hard in this setting to be consistent,
 in what we want to achieve...

00:17:42.779 --> 00:17:46.768
All of this said about video and how challenging it is...

00:17:46.768 --> 00:17:48.521
I am aware it's a great advertisement!

00:17:48.521 --> 00:17:51.795
We're also still looking for new video makers, 
that can join&nbsp;this team!

00:17:51.795 --> 00:17:53.987
Because, video is an important part of this project.

00:17:53.987 --> 00:17:57.068
And, we really want to make sure we&nbsp;deliver 
good videos each week.

00:17:57.068 --> 00:17:58.442
So, we could use a hand

00:17:58.442 --> 00:18:01.258
If you want to help out, there's a link below to sign up.

00:18:01.543 --> 00:18:04.601
And, we could also use some help for people subtitling the videos!

00:18:04.601 --> 00:18:06.715
We also have&nbsp;a little team for that now remotely!

00:18:06.715 --> 00:18:08.902
So, you can also go to the link below to see.

00:18:08.902 --> 00:18:11.985
And then, you can&nbsp;join these guys to help out editing the videos!

00:18:14.997 --> 00:18:17.208
Anyway, those were our current&nbsp;challenges!

00:18:17.208 --> 00:18:21.939
Next, we're going to do a Q&amp;A,
 where we're going to answer some of you guys' questions.

00:18:25.329 --> 00:18:27.870
- What is the most exciting project for&nbsp;
this season?

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:29.620
Most exciting project...

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.430
The lagoon obviously!

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:33.500
The yellow van!

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.754
Probably, Level 2 house!

00:18:35.754 --> 00:18:37.763
The new toilet!

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:41.320
The lagoon!

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:44.744
The whole season is exciting!

00:18:44.744 --> 00:18:46.229
The lagoon!

00:18:46.920 --> 00:18:48.632
Well, of course, it's the yellow van.

00:18:48.632 --> 00:18:51.700
This is a house on wheels!

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:53.247
The Level 2 housing...

00:18:53.247 --> 00:18:54.724
I think Level&nbsp;2 housing.

00:18:54.724 --> 00:18:55.704
I don't know...

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:59.637
- Where do you get all your money from, 
and what about food supplies?

00:18:59.637 --> 00:19:04.039
The money for building all the cool stuff, 
comes from YouTube and Patreon.

00:19:04.641 --> 00:19:09.426
Our food supplies&nbsp;come from four sources mainly.

00:19:09.426 --> 00:19:12.914
Which, is a small farm, run by somebody called Nuno.

00:19:12.914 --> 00:19:16.219
A bigger farm,&nbsp;run by two people called Nuno, incidentally.

00:19:16.884 --> 00:19:21.361
And, two bulk shops, which supply us with different goods.

00:19:21.968 --> 00:19:24.350
- Can you show us your video editing setup?

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.112
Here it is!

00:19:30.555 --> 00:19:32.673
- What's the most useful tool for sanding?

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:34.395
Well, it depends.

00:19:34.395 --> 00:19:40.979
If we are doing big jobs, or like rough jobs,
 we use the belt sander with 80 grit&nbsp;sandpaper.

00:19:41.581 --> 00:19:49.089
And, if we are doing like little surfaces, 
or more detail sanding, it's the orbital sander.

00:19:49.089 --> 00:19:55.002
With sanding paper of 80, 120, till 180 we go.

00:19:55.002 --> 00:19:57.165
So, yeah, that's what we use.

00:19:57.165 --> 00:20:00.872
- Regarding dogs, are&nbsp;there permanent residents or temporary?

00:20:00.872 --> 00:20:02.657
- Do they eat vegan food during the week?

00:20:03.182 --> 00:20:06.812
For now, Chester and I are staying for the whole season.

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:10.809
At least, he's enjoying himself more than anyone here.

00:20:10.809 --> 00:20:14.219
And, he just eats normal dog food during the whole week.

00:20:14.662 --> 00:20:15.934
- Vegan, or not vegan?

00:20:15.934 --> 00:20:16.832
Not vegan.

00:20:17.022 --> 00:20:22.692
- About energy expansion, will you&nbsp;wait until you have
 one year of data, or you will do something sooner?

00:20:22.692 --> 00:20:28.081
Now, we have a year worth of data&nbsp;
of our solar consumption and solar production.

00:20:28.271 --> 00:20:30.753
So, we are already working on it!

00:20:30.753 --> 00:20:33.654
But, as I said before&nbsp;this is a temporary setup...

00:20:33.654 --> 00:20:39.597
So, we need to combine a bit of temporary setup,
with the data we have, with the&nbsp;solutions we can apply now.

00:20:40.389 --> 00:20:43.269
- How does the camp deal with unavoidable garbage?

00:20:43.269 --> 00:20:51.064
Despite our best effort&nbsp;to reduce our waste, 
there are still some of the waste, that we don't know how to deal with...

00:20:51.064 --> 00:20:58.950
So, we&nbsp;still have around like 2 kilos of waste, 
going to the 'landfill' every week.

00:20:58.950 --> 00:21:02.398
- How do you prioritize&nbsp;or use advice from the YouTube comments?

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:07.882
We don't have a system to prioritize any YouTube comments,&nbsp;
or advice we get through the platform.

00:21:08.829 --> 00:21:10.134
Sometimes, we read things...

00:21:10.134 --> 00:21:10.990
Makes sense.

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:12.258
So, we apply them.

00:21:12.258 --> 00:21:16.103
Sometimes, we don't really see a way to address them...

00:21:16.103 --> 00:21:20.166
- Can I, as a builder, come with my children,
 or&nbsp;is it too dangerous for little kids?

00:21:20.520 --> 00:21:24.306
The Kamp is not yet very children-proof...

00:21:24.559 --> 00:21:26.308
It's at a very raw state, and very 'beginner'.

00:21:27.385 --> 00:21:31.021
Hopefully, in&nbsp;the future, we will have a positive answer to that!

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:34.228
- Has the camp considered getting a resident goat or two?

00:21:34.513 --> 00:21:36.137
So, for now, we have enough people.

00:21:36.137 --> 00:21:38.458
I think they act like goats sometimes...

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:42.592
- Have you considered&nbsp;planting fruit trees, 
or wild flowers on your land, with some beehives?

00:21:42.592 --> 00:21:44.533
- So, you can produce your&nbsp;own honey?

00:21:44.533 --> 00:21:45.680
I think about it a lot...

00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:48.471
Especially, when I see all the orange trees 
around here, in the neighborhood...

00:21:49.231 --> 00:21:50.547
We're going to plant more this year!

00:21:51.244 --> 00:21:54.952
But, if you actually want to see more about it,
 we already explained this in Episode 74.

00:21:55.320 --> 00:21:57.599
- How do you communicate with each other on&nbsp;your land?

00:21:57.599 --> 00:21:58.834
- Do you use walkie-talkies?

00:21:58.834 --> 00:22:01.097
- Are you planning to put glassfiber?

00:22:01.350 --> 00:22:03.646
Well, for now, we shout quite a bit...

00:22:03.646 --> 00:22:09.767
But, we have a walkie-talkie to communicate,
 between the kitchen and the&nbsp;office.

00:22:09.767 --> 00:22:13.072
We don't intend to lay glassfiber yet...

00:22:13.072 --> 00:22:15.905
Maybe a couple of seasons into the future.

00:22:16.317 --> 00:22:17.785
- Are&nbsp;you residents in Portugal?

00:22:17.785 --> 00:22:20.145
- Do you need permissions to live in a van on the land?

00:22:20.145 --> 00:22:23.276
Yeah, some&nbsp;of us are residents in Portugal!

00:22:25.303 --> 00:22:31.770
I don't think you need a permission to live in a van,&nbsp;
if you're having a van on your own private land.

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:33.626
- How's about the highway sounds?

00:22:34.418 --> 00:22:39.972
Still there,&nbsp;but I notice them less, for some reason!

00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:41.391
Which, is good...

00:22:41.391 --> 00:22:44.090
- How do you get all of your ideas&nbsp;for your projects?

00:22:44.090 --> 00:22:45.826
Well, this is the easy part.

00:22:45.826 --> 00:22:47.319
Many, many things to do...

00:22:47.319 --> 00:22:49.781
Even YouTube comments have so&nbsp;many ideas.

00:22:50.224 --> 00:22:52.867
I think, the challenge is more: "How do you filter them?"

00:22:52.867 --> 00:22:54.733
Which one do you take on?

00:22:54.955 --> 00:22:57.571
- Has Wes Anderson&nbsp;being volunteering with the filming?

00:22:57.951 --> 00:22:59.923
No, not so far!

00:23:01.693 --> 00:23:03.196
- What do you think about caravans?

00:23:03.196 --> 00:23:06.101
I don't like the&nbsp;materials they are made out of...

00:23:06.101 --> 00:23:09.560
Usually fiberglass, plastics, not durable...

00:23:09.560 --> 00:23:12.464
They change with the time, and they are bit ugly...

00:23:12.464 --> 00:23:15.281
And, they don't really fit our setup that good...

00:23:15.598 --> 00:23:18.502
- How much did the land&nbsp;cost, when you initially purchased it?

00:23:18.882 --> 00:23:23.783
The price was close to 100.000 euros, for 10 hectares of&nbsp;land.

00:23:24.322 --> 00:23:27.061
- How do you organize healthcare for your community members?

00:23:27.061 --> 00:23:29.242
I don't think we figured out&nbsp;this topic...

00:23:29.242 --> 00:23:32.857
Most people come temporary, 
so they have their own healthcare system.

00:23:32.857 --> 00:23:34.525
In their own land, where they're from...

00:23:34.778 --> 00:23:38.670
For the long-term members: to be figured out, I would say...

00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:41.556
- What do you guys&nbsp;do for hobbies, or downtime?

00:23:41.556 --> 00:23:45.178
Everybody does kind of their own thing, I'd say.

00:23:45.178 --> 00:23:47.782
But, there is a game&nbsp;night each week...

00:23:47.782 --> 00:23:49.448
There is a movie night each week...

00:23:49.448 --> 00:23:54.737
So, there's opportunities where we gather
 in groups, and have such activities.

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:57.608
- Can you sustain yourself at any kind of income?

00:23:57.608 --> 00:24:00.606
So, this question&nbsp;doesn't really feel clear...

00:24:00.606 --> 00:24:05.957
If I understood well, YouTube revenue is not a lot...

00:24:06.400 --> 00:24:10.793
But, it's enough&nbsp;to keep the project running, 
and to make the projects happen, and stuff like that.

00:24:10.793 --> 00:24:20.320
And then, for our personal sustaining income wise,
we do have side jobs, or remote jobs.

00:24:20.513 --> 00:24:21.775
- How&nbsp;do you split work?

00:24:21.775 --> 00:24:22.793
- Is there a schedule?

00:24:22.793 --> 00:24:25.903
- How much work does one person do, 
when it's staying in the Kamp?

00:24:26.346 --> 00:24:28.965
Okay, so, we have a schedule -- very lovely!

00:24:28.965 --> 00:24:33.764
We meet every Monday morning, 
and every Friday&nbsp;afternoon together.

00:24:35.063 --> 00:24:37.168
Inbetween, we just make sure that we feel good

00:24:37.168 --> 00:24:41.720
So, we are giving the energy&nbsp;we can give,
 and we rest whenever we need to rest.

00:24:42.180 --> 00:24:45.078
- Do people with any kind of disability live at Project Kamp?

00:24:45.078 --> 00:24:48.907
- And if no, do you have plans to integrate people
 with disabilities of any kind?

00:24:49.319 --> 00:24:52.972
So far, nobody&nbsp;with disabilities came to Project Kamp to help.

00:24:53.340 --> 00:24:58.436
We are open, but of course, 
it depends on the&nbsp;limitation the disability will bring...

00:24:58.816 --> 00:25:02.068
Like, nowadays, we are not wheelchair proof.

00:25:02.575 --> 00:25:03.970
But, it depends...

00:25:03.970 --> 00:25:05.722
Depends on the disability.

00:25:06.165 --> 00:25:09.858
- Have you thought to start recycling,
 and creating plastic products for&nbsp;sale from there?

00:25:10.460 --> 00:25:12.932
So, so far, we don't sell anything from the Kamp...

00:25:13.344 --> 00:25:16.092
We don't have big machinery in&nbsp;the country and recycled plastic...

00:25:16.092 --> 00:25:21.273
And, luckily, we don't have many plastic streams in the Kamp either.

00:25:21.273 --> 00:25:24.433
- What is everyone's favorite thing about being at Project Kamp?

00:25:24.433 --> 00:25:29.026
The favorite thing about Project&nbsp;Kamp is the people.

00:25:29.026 --> 00:25:30.044
The people.

00:25:30.044 --> 00:25:31.695
Yeah, the human beings!

00:25:31.695 --> 00:25:33.157
I would say the people!

00:25:33.157 --> 00:25:34.713
So many talented people!

00:25:34.713 --> 00:25:36.880
Seeing everyone growing personally.

00:25:37.102 --> 00:25:38.150
The vision.

00:25:40.121 --> 00:25:42.760
 

00:25:42.960 --> 00:25:46.386
All of the lovely dinners that are cooked for us!

00:25:46.386 --> 00:25:48.260
And, all of the really friendly people!

00:25:48.260 --> 00:25:50.005
Doing everything outside, and living outside.

00:25:50.005 --> 00:25:54.774
It gives me the freedom to&nbsp;do what I love,
 in the way I like it.

00:25:54.774 --> 00:25:58.265
Being part of something bigger, I think.

00:25:58.835 --> 00:26:00.059
I like every day!

00:26:00.376 --> 00:26:02.040
Life to life, day to day!

00:26:02.040 --> 00:26:04.275
Fuck Javier, I don't know man...

00:26:08.580 --> 00:26:11.120
Feeling that I do something useful, I think.

00:26:11.753 --> 00:26:12.760
I like&nbsp;that.

00:26:13.140 --> 00:26:16.205
You're not gonna get me with this video Javier...

00:26:16.320 --> 00:26:20.384
- Do you avoid animal products,
considering their lack of sustainability?

00:26:20.880 --> 00:26:24.923
It's one reason, but it's&nbsp;actually a super complex answer to give...

00:26:25.747 --> 00:26:30.085
Last season, we had a video a bit more in depth.

00:26:30.085 --> 00:26:35.005
Our decision&nbsp;making around eating,
 and maybe you can check that in that video.

00:26:35.005 --> 00:26:37.818
- Have you tried the burnt wood method&nbsp;of conservation?

00:26:38.420 --> 00:26:39.607
So, yeah, we tried!

00:26:39.607 --> 00:26:41.508
You can check it in update 72!

00:26:41.508 --> 00:26:43.777
Last update of Season 2!

00:26:44.727 --> 00:26:46.000
And, here it is!

00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:48.281
Seems like it's doing well...

00:26:50.752 --> 00:26:51.926
Let's see in the longer run.

00:26:52.623 --> 00:26:55.062
- How much&nbsp;did the tent, and deck project cost?

00:26:55.410 --> 00:26:58.308
240 euros for the deck, built here on location.

00:26:58.308 --> 00:26:59.853
Sourcing this local&nbsp;sawmill...

00:26:59.853 --> 00:27:03.082
And, 600 euro from Eva and Kaegh. 

00:27:03.082 --> 00:27:06.780
Canvas, materials, prototyping, etcetera.

00:27:06.780 --> 00:27:11.280
But, you can still&nbsp;find all the information related to this project.

00:27:11.280 --> 00:27:13.434
In the research topic, that you can find below.

00:27:13.434 --> 00:27:16.570
- Regarding the tent, could it be made with Precious Plastic beams?

00:27:17.109 --> 00:27:19.933
Yes, it could be made with recycled&nbsp;plastic beams!

00:27:19.933 --> 00:27:22.249
This is a prototype, but a cool idea!

00:27:22.760 --> 00:27:24.235
- How's your fireproofing going?

00:27:24.615 --> 00:27:26.630
- Have you planned&nbsp;to dig some more ponds?

00:27:26.630 --> 00:27:28.157
Yes, we're working on this!

00:27:28.157 --> 00:27:30.000
Clearing a lot of mimosa!

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:32.000
Ponds: still in progress...

00:27:32.520 --> 00:27:34.268
- What is the main goal of the project?

00:27:34.520 --> 00:27:38.201
This is&nbsp;always a tough question, 
because I think we really don't know...

00:27:38.201 --> 00:27:40.646
We sort of have a vague idea.

00:27:40.646 --> 00:27:44.043
I think&nbsp;the goal in the short term is to set up a Basekamp.

00:27:44.043 --> 00:27:49.350
Invite people, set up infrastructure, so that we&nbsp;can
properly figure out what our long-term goal is.

00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:54.243
But, yeah, it's roughly something about figuring&nbsp;
out how to live sustainable.

00:27:54.243 --> 00:27:57.568
And, share all the documentations, and drawings online, for free.

00:27:57.568 --> 00:27:59.685
So, the&nbsp;people all around the world can replicate it.

00:28:00.128 --> 00:28:03.667
But, the details of that are still to be figured&nbsp;out...

00:28:04.047 --> 00:28:07.067
- What happened with the plastic roof built in Update 40?

00:28:07.067 --> 00:28:11.300
- And, why didn't you use recycled&nbsp;plastic 
to build a roof on top of the container?

00:28:12.345 --> 00:28:15.837
The recycled roof is still there, but still in a&nbsp; testing mode.

00:28:15.837 --> 00:28:18.787
So, we don't want to make two tests at the same time...

00:28:18.787 --> 00:28:25.939
It's going well, but we don't&nbsp;feel comfy enough,
 to extend these tests to other constructions...

00:28:26.382 --> 00:28:30.560
- What is the ratio you try to hit,
&nbsp;between longevity and repairability?

00:28:30.560 --> 00:28:34.620
I would say more repairability than longevity,
 but longevity&nbsp;very high too.

00:28:34.620 --> 00:28:38.367
Trying to not use new materials,
 trying to reuse as much as we can...

00:28:38.367 --> 00:28:45.035
And, use much&nbsp;natural materials as we can,
 to avoid all plastic, glues...

00:28:45.035 --> 00:28:49.555
These kind of things are not&nbsp;repairable, and not natural...

00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:53.418
- How many people do work in the project, 
and where is the landscape located?

00:28:53.418 --> 00:28:58.778
So, at the moment, we are 20, 
but we will become 25.

00:28:59.360 --> 00:29:01.930
We will also become less, always changing!

00:29:02.373 --> 00:29:06.116
And, the project is located in central Portugal.

00:29:06.845 --> 00:29:10.165
- Are there any language barriers in the Kamp,
 and&nbsp;what is the main language?

00:29:10.165 --> 00:29:16.809
No, there is a bit of a barrier maybe, with some people,
 that don't&nbsp;speak Portuguese to speak with the neighbors.

00:29:16.980 --> 00:29:19.140
But, yeah, the main language is English.

00:29:20.040 --> 00:29:23.418
- What sort of data are you capturing about the project these days?

00:29:23.418 --> 00:29:26.968
- And, what&nbsp;data do you wish 
you were captured that you haven't done yet?

00:29:27.380 --> 00:29:28.704
We have some data on&nbsp;
the website

00:29:28.704 --> 00:29:34.145
Where we currently gather solar, 
internet usage, and water usage.

00:29:34.583 --> 00:29:37.760
What I&nbsp;would like to get is poop buckets!

00:29:39.090 --> 00:29:41.475
To weigh the amount of poop, that comes out of us.

00:29:41.475 --> 00:29:43.638
I would really be curious for that!

00:29:44.018 --> 00:29:47.427
And, a more practical one is actually the water level in the well.

00:29:47.427 --> 00:29:50.836
That it goes up and down that, 
and that we can see that it's&nbsp;not too low in summer...

00:29:50.836 --> 00:29:52.455
But, the poop buckets is more fun!

00:29:52.772 --> 00:29:55.710
- How do you plan to dig out the&nbsp;pond above the waterfall?

00:29:55.710 --> 00:29:56.597
Good question!

00:29:57.523 --> 00:29:58.573
We already got the answer!

00:29:58.573 --> 00:30:00.870
You will see it soon, in an&nbsp;upcoming update!

00:30:01.250 --> 00:30:03.448
- Was there a Kamp Eurovision party?

00:30:03.448 --> 00:30:05.200
 

00:30:05.200 --> 00:30:06.880
 

00:30:06.880 --> 00:30:09.450
- How do you keep Adrian from eating all the&nbsp;
bread?

00:30:09.450 --> 00:30:11.708
They cannot keep me, Joseph.

00:30:11.708 --> 00:30:14.533
- How many people in total will be living in Project&nbsp;Kamp?

00:30:14.533 --> 00:30:15.640
- And, what is the limit?

00:30:15.640 --> 00:30:20.126
Throughout the season, the limit capacity,
of what we have right now,&nbsp;is 25.

00:30:20.728 --> 00:30:25.978
We never tried it out with so many people,
and we will see how the systems will be&nbsp;functioning.

00:30:26.326 --> 00:30:33.241
In the future, we don't really have a very clear idea
 how many people will be living at&nbsp;the Kamp.

00:30:33.241 --> 00:30:35.182
Maybe around 50?

00:30:35.752 --> 00:30:38.805
- Support from India: what is the purpose of doing this?

00:30:38.805 --> 00:30:42.380
So, I think on the&nbsp;one hand we're trying 
just to do something useful...

00:30:42.380 --> 00:30:47.550
For what we think is useful for the planet
at the moment, and future generations to come.

00:30:47.925 --> 00:30:52.345
But, also making sure, personally for ourselves,
that it's like fun along the way.

00:30:52.345 --> 00:30:56.095
And, that it doesn't become a very annoying, boring, heavy thing...

00:30:56.095 --> 00:30:57.848
So, I&nbsp;think those two things!

00:30:57.848 --> 00:31:01.695
Doing something useful, but making sure we enjoy
 the road to get there&nbsp;as well.

00:31:02.138 --> 00:31:03.803
that's the purpose of this

00:31:03.803 --> 00:31:08.871
And, for the coming plans: in Update 74, you can see all the&nbsp;things
we're going to do in the coming year.

